skStop", "WebFetch", "Write", "mcp__rwe-search__search_literature"], "tokens": {"cache_write_1h_input": 2088, "cache_write_5m_input": 0, "cache_write_input": 2088, "cached_input": 67506, "input": 69596, "output": 187}, "context": {"bytes": {"conversation": 100667, "other": 423, "system": 30811, "tool_definitions": 14397, "tool_results": 85091}, "measure": "json-utf8-bytes", "total_bytes": 231389}, "gateway_set": ["thinking.display"], "web_search": false, "web_searches": 0, "calls": {"Bash": 1}}}, {"id": "09509360-eb25-5c05-ab09-3f4e7c599d99", "at": 1795634112.324759, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 4514, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "73197538b27ac9f4b9b10091b3050342", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "5ad80edc-4443-5ee4-adff-a72b36048f51", "at": 1795634113.0867171, "until": 1795634113.1036654, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 4515, "layer": "worker", "category": "thinking", "kind": "session.agent_thought_chunk", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": null, "execution_id": "73197538b27ac9f4b9b10091b3050342", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "thinking", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "thinking (6 chunks, content withheld)"}, {"id": "224097b8-2f9e-554e-9064-9f65326391a2", "at": 1795634113.1062336, "until": 1795634114.8845732, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 4521, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "73197538b27ac9f4b9b10091b3050342", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01LEPB91EtTjvXwYJCTsKDN7", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian/ideawiki && git remote set-url origin $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/idea-repo.wiki.git && timeout 120 git pull -q; git log --oneline | head -3; grep -n -i -E \"cell|core|draws|replicate|acceptance|supported\" Brief.md | cut -c1-600", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/ideawiki && git remote set-url origin $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/idea-repo.wiki.git && timeout 120 git pull -q; git log --oneline | head -3; grep -n -i -E \"cell|core|draws|replicate|acceptance|supported\" Brief.md | cut -c1-600"]], "output": "```console\n0be35f3 Brief revision 4: P5 acceptance rule per target with null simulation, cell budget, edge-noise slice, DM bias per design, corner check, SNR\n6547693 Brief: leverage formula written out\n8609381 Brief r2: separate variance and bias drivers, two-part diagnostic with acceptance rule, tiered baselines\n15:- P1. Where residuals are independent with variance σ², Var(τ̂) ≈ σ² L / n (OLS leverage; textbook, stated as the baseline, not the finding). The test is the *departure*: fit log-RMSE on log n, log d, log p(1−p) with CIs, on graphs where the iid formula is expected to hold (ER/SBM, Bernoulli) and where not (BA hubs, cluster designs, degree-correlated baselines, 2-hop features with shared neighbours); report where σ²L/n over- or under-states the realised variance and by what factor (an effective-n). Noise model fixed: iid Gaussian ε with σ a multiple of the SD of the noise-free\n19:- P4 (treatment probability): variance minimised at p = ½ (algebra, L); bias minimised at p = ½ to second order, with the minimiser shifting to p < ½ for exponentially saturating responses (g''<0, g'''>0) by the third-order term and the reverse for the mirror response. The test is whether realised bias/RMSE follows this, on p ∈ {0.1, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 0.9} (core cells).\n23:- P5: a two-part diagnostic computable from one experiment: (i) leverage L (predicts the *variance* part), (ii) a specification-disagreement term S plus the raw corner distance outside the observed exposure support (predicts the *bias* part). S = spread of τ̂ across a pre-listed ladder of specifications (linear, +quadratic exposure, spline in exposure, +count, +2-hop), measured as the deviation of each *other* specification from the pre-chosen reporting specification (Chin: own z + fraction). Pre-registered benchmarks it must beat: mean degree alone, p(1−p) alone, n·p(1−p)/d, the est\n24:  - *Part (i), variance.* Target: the realised variance of τ̂ over assignment and noise draws in a cell. Tested **across cells and graph draws**, not within a cell: within a cell L barely varies over assignment draws, so a within-cell rank correlation of L with |error| can be ≈ 0 when the theory is exactly right, and is not used for L. What is reported: the R² of log realised variance on log L (+ log n, log σ²), against the benchmarks, and the departure ratio realised/(σ²L/n).\n25:  - *Part (ii), bias.* Target: |realised bias| = |mean error over draws| in a cell. Predictors: S̄ (cell mean) and the raw corner distance × estimated curvature. To avoid using the same draws on both sides, S̄ is computed on a random half of the draws and the bias on the other half.\n26:  - *Within-cell test (S and the bootstrap SE only).* On the **centred error** (error − cell mean error), because the cell bias is constant across draws. S is partly mechanical within a cell (a draw whose reporting-spec τ̂ lies far out moves S), so the within-cell Spearman of S with |centred error| is read against a **null simulation**: the same cell, outcomes generated from the reporting specification itself (correct spec, noise only), where there is no extrapolation bias and the true S–error association is only the mechanical one. The statistic is the observed within-cell Spearman m\n27:  - *Combined score.* Headline: leave-one-mechanism-out and leave-one-graph-family-out R² of log-RMSE of the combined score against each benchmark, **on top of** the two separate tests above.\n28:  - *Resampling and power.* Cells within a mechanism (and graph draws within a family) are strongly dependent, so the CI resamples at the **mechanism / family level**, not over cells. With 6 mechanisms and 4–6 families this has low power; the analysis reports the held-out R² gain **per held-out group**, so no single mechanism or family carries the verdict.\n29:  - *Acceptance rule (fixed before running).* **Supported** if (1) the pooled held-out R² gain over the best benchmark is ≥ 0.05 with the group-level bootstrap CI excluding 0, (2) the gain is positive i\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "96915f51-ff89-53ed-9401-1f6efbf13ffb", "at": 1795634113.567681, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 4523, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "73197538b27ac9f4b9b10091b3050342", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "c59a45ef-b6ef-5385-93e0-8b6044623e66", "at": 1795634113.5728166, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 4524, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "73197538b27ac9f4b9b10091b3050342", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "1e663d78-9cff-5e13-8045-66f0e422f29b", "at": 1795634113.5766006, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 4525, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "73197538b27ac9f4b9b10091b3050342", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "2691a1cf-f19c-5871-9fbb-717b7915af98", "at": 1795634113.6350212, "clock": "hos